# sepolicy.rule — intentionally EMPTY at v0.1.
#
# Policy is added here ONLY when a real on-device `avc: denied` proves the daemon
# needs it, and each rule is scoped to the daemon domain — never a broad
# permissive mode and never untrusted_app-scoped. Todo 1 ran the daemon context
# discovery as read-only; any required rule lands here with the denial that
# justified it recorded in docs/.
